      "id": 1,
      "text": "Furman derives its name from Lizzie Furman, a formerly enslaved woman who donated land for the town's first railroad depot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/furman_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lizzie Furman was known locally as Mum for the herbal remedies she provided to the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/furman_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Furman was formally incorporated as a town on March 21, 1911, following settlement during the Reconstruction era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/furman_south_carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Furman lies within the Lower Savannah River Basin, where local streams and wetlands influence the region's ecosystem.",
